{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Manual: Deploy Activation Handler",
  "description": "Manually trigger activation handler deployment using Kiro MCP servers",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "🎯 **Manual Activation Handler Deployment**\n\nI want to manually deploy the activation handler. Please execute this Kiro-powered deployment workflow:\n\n**🔍 Step 1: Pre-Deployment Assessment**\n1. Check the current status of `src/lambda/activation-handler/index.ts`\n2. Show me any uncommitted changes in the activation handler\n3. Verify the activation handler code compiles without errors\n4. Ask me to confirm the deployment target environment (dev/staging/prod)\n\n**🧪 Step 2: Code Quality Validation**\n5. Run TypeScript build: `npm run build`\n6. Run linting: `npm run lint` (focus on activation handler)\n7. Run tests: `npm test`\n8. If any validation fails, stop and report issues\n9. If all pass, proceed to deployment\n\n**📝 Step 3: Git Operations (if needed)**\n10. If there are uncommitted changes:\n    - Show me the changes with git diff\n    - Ask for a commit message\n    - Stage and commit: `git add src/lambda/activation-handler/ && git commit -m \"[message]\"`\n    - Push to GitHub: `git push origin recovered`\n11. If already committed, proceed to deployment\n\n**🔧 Step 4: AWS Deployment via MCP**\n12. Use AWS Operations MCP server to:\n    - Get current status of `FOD-Compute-dev-ActivationHandler`\n    - Show me the current function configuration\n    - Check the last modified timestamp\n13. Trigger GitHub Actions workflow specifically for activation handler\n14. Monitor deployment progress using AWS Operations MCP\n15. Provide real-time updates on deployment status\n\n**✅ Step 5: Deployment Verification**\n16. Use AWS Operations MCP to verify:\n    - Lambda function was successfully updated\n    - Function is in 'Active' state\n    - No immediate errors in CloudWatch\n    - Function configuration is correct\n17. Get the updated function's ARN and last modified time\n18. Show me the deployment completion confirmation\n\n**🧪 Step 6: Post-Deployment Testing**\n19. Use Snapdragon Simulator MCP to:\n    - Test a sample activation flow\n    - Verify the simulator can communicate with updated function\n    - Check that activation logic works as expected\n20. Use AWS Operations MCP to:\n    - Check CloudWatch logs for any errors\n    - Verify function metrics look healthy\n    - Confirm no throttling or timeout issues\n\n**📊 Step 7: Health Check Report**\n21. Generate a comprehensive health report:\n    - Function status: Active/Error\n    - Recent invocations: Count and success rate\n    - Error rate: Last 5 minutes\n    - Average duration: Performance metrics\n    - Memory utilization: Resource usage\n22. Show me any warnings or recommendations\n\n**📋 Step 8: Documentation**\n23. Use GitHub MCP server to:\n    - Create a deployment record issue:\n      - Title: \"Manual Deployment: Activation Handler [timestamp]\"\n      - Body: Include all deployment details and verification results\n      - Labels: ['deployment', 'activation-handler', 'manual']\n24. Ask if I want to update any documentation\n25. Close any related GitHub issues if this deployment resolves them\n\n**🎉 Step 9: Completion Summary**\n26. Provide final deployment summary:\n    - ✅ Deployment Status: SUCCESS/FAILED\n    - 📊 Function ARN: [full ARN]\n    - 🕐 Deployment Time: [timestamp]\n    - 📈 Health Status: [metrics summary]\n    - 🔗 GitHub Actions: [workflow URL]\n    - 📝 Documentation: [GitHub issue URL]\n    - 🧪 Test Results: [simulator test results]\n\n**🚨 Error Handling**\n- Stop immediately if code quality checks fail\n- Provide detailed error messages and remediation steps\n- Create GitHub issues for any deployment failures\n- Offer rollback options if deployment fails\n- Log all errors for debugging\n\n**🎯 Key Features of This Kiro-Powered Deployment:**\n- Uses MCP servers instead of traditional scripts\n- Comprehensive validation and testing\n- Real-time monitoring and feedback\n- Automatic documentation and issue creation\n- Integration with Snapdragon simulator for testing\n- Full AWS operations via MCP\n- GitHub integration for tracking\n\nPlease execute this manual deployment workflow and guide me through each step. Use the MCP servers to perform all operations and keep me informed of the progress."
  },
  "workspaceFolderName": "snapdragon-fod-aws",
  "shortName": "manual-activation-deploy"
}